  "term": "programming",
  "definition": "In this context, programming refers to neurolinguistic programming: a set of models about how communication and subjective experience affect each other. It uses ordered techniques based on those models to try to alter a person’s internal representations and the behavior patterns linked to interactions among the brain, language, and body.",
